      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:3:13:7",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُهُ يَقُولُ إِنَّ النَّفْسَ إِذَا وَقَعَتْ فِي الْحَلْقِ أَتَاهُ مَلَكٌ فَقَالَ لَهُ يَا هَذَا أَوْ يَا فُلَانُ أَمَّا مَا كُنْتَ تَرْجُو فَأْيَسْ مِنْهُ وَ هُوَ الرُّجُوعُ إِلَى الدُّنْيَا وَ أَمَّا مَا كُنْتَ تَخَافُ فَقَدْ أَمِنْتَ مِنْهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd Bin Ziyad, from Al Hassan Bin Muhammad Al Kindy, from someone else, from AbanBin Usman, from Aamir Bin Abdullah Bin Juza’at, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, said, ‘I heard him<sup>asws</sup> saying: ‘When the soul comes to be in the throat, an Angel comes over to him and says to him: ‘O you!’, or ‘O so and so! As for what you were hoping for, so despair from it’, and it is the returning to the world, ‘And as for what you were fearing, so you are (now) secured from it’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Humayd ibn Ziyad has narrated from al-Hassan ibn Muhammad al-Kindiy from more than one person from Aban ibn ‘Uthman from ‘Amir ibn ‘Abd Allah ibn Judha‘ah who has said the following: “I heard abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, say, ‘When a soul reaches the throat, an angel comes and says to him, “O you, - or so and so - what you had hoped for, be certain, is of no avail to you, meaning returning to the worldly life, but you have become safe from whatever you were afraid of.’”” "
        ]
      }
    },
